WEBVTT

1
00:01:45.724 --> 00:01:47.634
What a humiliation.

2
00:01:50.284 --> 00:01:53.276
A lot of unhappiness
 around the Bernabeu tonight,

3
00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:57.039
a lot of it directed at Gavin Harris.
 Came out as a hero,

4
00:01:57.124 --> 00:01:59.035
he's being called a donkey tonight.

5
00:02:12.884 --> 00:02:16.399
Ronaldinho seals it
 with a brilliant third.

6
00:02:22.484 --> 00:02:25.794
Boy, do they need
 some inspiration from somewhere.

7
00:02:30.684 --> 00:02:34.677
And now it's Munez. And we
 haven't seen too much of him today.

8
00:02:34.764 --> 00:02:38.120
Trying a give-and-go here
 with Alan Shearer.

9
00:02:38.204 --> 00:02:40.877
What a great run by Munez!

10
00:02:42.284 --> 00:02:46.994
Unbelievable!
 Newcastle's newest and youngest player

11
00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:50.042
gives the fans a brand-new song to sing.

12
00:02:53.844 --> 00:02:57.234
He's got support to his right.

13
00:02:58.324 --> 00:03:00.315
Stephen Carr.

14
00:03:01.084 --> 00:03:03.040
A great header!

15
00:03:04.444 --> 00:03:06.275
And a goal!

16
00:03:06.364 --> 00:03:08.878
It's a dream start for Newcastle!

17
00:03:50.004 --> 00:03:52.802
- OK.
 - What about the rose petals?

18
00:03:52.884 --> 00:03:56.399
About bloody time. Can we have
 the red rose petals, but in that...?

19
00:04:05.684 --> 00:04:07.675
- Gotta get back to work.
 - Hey, babe.

20
00:04:07.764 --> 00:04:10.153
- OK. Hello.
 - Hey.

21
00:04:10.244 --> 00:04:12.235
Just no fuss.

22
00:04:12.324 --> 00:04:14.554
I've got to go,
 but I will see you Tuesday.

23
00:04:14.644 --> 00:04:17.112
- All right. Bye.
 - Bye-bye.

24
00:04:18.084 --> 00:04:21.872
San, it's ten of 5.00. The meeting
 with the wedding planner was at 4.00.

25
00:04:21.964 --> 00:04:24.717
Sorry, babe. I just...
 I lost track of time.

26
00:04:24.804 --> 00:04:27.841
- We do this together.
 - What do I know about flowers?

27
00:04:27.924 --> 00:04:30.518
As long as you show up,
 I'll be happy.

28
00:04:30.604 --> 00:04:33.118
You Latin boys are so cheeky.
 Do you know that?

29
00:04:33.204 --> 00:04:36.037
- Are you gonna show up?
 - I might, if you're lucky.

30
00:04:37.004 --> 00:04:39.279
Oh, no. Go and have a shower. You stink.

31
00:04:53.364 --> 00:04:55.002
It's time for a toast, I think.

32
00:04:55.084 --> 00:04:58.281
To your new home, may all your ups
 and downs be in the bedroom.

33
00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.195
Mom!

34
00:05:01.724 --> 00:05:05.000
You might want to be careful, Santi.
 Look where it got me!

35
00:05:05.084 --> 00:05:06.995
You're lucky I let you get near me.

36
00:05:07.084 --> 00:05:10.633
- How about the extra hot vindaloo?
 - Sounds good.

37
00:05:10.724 --> 00:05:13.761
Have consideration.
 I'm the one who has to sleep with him.

38
00:05:13.844 --> 00:05:17.154
It sounds good.

39
00:05:17.244 --> 00:05:19.041
- Hello, stranger.
 - Hello.

40
00:05:19.124 --> 00:05:22.241
What happened?
 Did you lose me number?

41
00:05:22.324 --> 00:05:24.884
- Good timing. We're ordering.
 - Can I have a word?

42
00:05:24.964 --> 00:05:27.797
- Yeah, sure.
 - In private?

43
00:05:27.884 --> 00:05:29.317
Excuse us.

44
00:05:41.324 --> 00:05:42.882
Oh, my God.

45
00:05:44.044 --> 00:05:46.239
I've been on the phone for hours.

46
00:05:47.524 --> 00:05:49.276
Are they serious?

47
00:05:51.564 --> 00:05:53.077
They want to meet us.

48
00:06:07.604 --> 00:06:09.754
- Shtoom, though, OK?
 - Yeah.

49
00:06:10.244 --> 00:06:12.474
You've got two more years
 with Newcastle.

50
00:06:12.564 --> 00:06:15.317
The fans'll go mad.
 You're the best player.

51
00:06:15.404 --> 00:06:17.520
It's just a meeting.

52
00:06:17.604 --> 00:06:21.119
So when are they coming to meet us?

53
00:06:21.204 --> 00:06:24.879
They're not.
 I'm meeting them in Japan.

54
00:07:01.684 --> 00:07:04.676
The biggest football club on the planet.

55
00:07:04.764 --> 00:07:09.394
Nine times European champions.
 Twenty-nine Spanish League titles.

56
00:07:09.484 --> 00:07:13.033
Twelve Spanish Cups.
 One Super Cup.

57
00:07:13.764 --> 00:07:16.801
They come to Tokyo every summer,
 the whole squad.

58
00:07:16.884 --> 00:07:21.400
Beckham, Raul,
 Ronaldo, Roberto Carlos,

59
00:07:21.484 --> 00:07:25.716
Zidane, Harris, Munez.

60
00:07:54.644 --> 00:07:57.397
Won't be long, don't worry.

61
00:08:00.684 --> 00:08:02.515
Thank you for coming.

62
00:08:02.604 --> 00:08:04.435
- Santi, how are you?
 - Fine thank you.

63
00:08:04.524 --> 00:08:05.752
Welcome to this
 legendary football club.

64
00:08:06.884 --> 00:08:08.761
I wanted to introduce you
 to our coach.

65
00:08:08.844 --> 00:08:10.880
- Van der Merwe.
 - Pleased to meet you.

66
00:08:11.844 --> 00:08:14.961
- Sorry you had to come so fast.
 - That's fine.

67
00:08:15.044 --> 00:08:17.922
We want Santiago.
 We can make this work.

68
00:08:18.004 --> 00:08:21.883
We have to act quickly. The transfer
 window closes tomorrow at midnight.

69
00:08:21.964 --> 00:08:25.001
- I know. Let's vamoose.
 - OK. Come on.

70
00:08:28.444 --> 00:08:30.639
Just don't think about the money.

71
00:08:30.724 --> 00:08:34.637
You're gonna hate Madrid.
 They all speak bloody Spanish.

72
00:08:34.724 --> 00:08:36.203
- How's it going?
 - Good.

73
00:08:36.284 --> 00:08:38.639
- We haven't said yes yet.
 - What, are you mad?

74
00:08:38.724 --> 00:08:43.718
With ten percent you have your chest
 waxed and highlights. You're sorted.

75
00:08:43.804 --> 00:08:46.443
It's a big decision.
 Roz and I got this new house.

76
00:08:46.524 --> 00:08:48.992
You came halfway around
 the world for karaoke?

77
00:08:49.084 --> 00:08:52.042
No one says no to Real Madrid,
 you nutter.

78
00:08:52.124 --> 00:08:56.322
I don't wanna be on the bench like Owen.
 He's one of the best. I'd go crazy.

79
00:08:58.044 --> 00:08:59.557
- It's Dutch.
 - Gentlemen.

80
00:08:59.644 --> 00:09:01.839
Herr Van der Merwe.
 Can I get you a drink?

81
00:09:01.924 --> 00:09:05.280
Thank you. You're not
 giving any career advice, are you?

82
00:09:05.364 --> 00:09:07.798
He's pretending
 he's got a decision to make.

83
00:09:07.884 --> 00:09:09.715
I have some advice.

84
00:09:09.804 --> 00:09:11.635
First, you listen to your heart.

85
00:09:11.724 --> 00:09:14.796
Then you listen to your head.

86
00:09:14.884 --> 00:09:17.000
Then your wife will
 tell you what to do.

87
00:09:26.924 --> 00:09:28.915
You're OK, Mr lves.

88
00:09:34.124 --> 00:09:36.035
Sorry, doctor.

89
00:09:45.764 --> 00:09:46.799
No comment!

90
00:09:48.644 --> 00:09:51.204
Don't leave, Santi! Don't leave!

91
00:09:52.164 --> 00:09:55.361
[Woman on TV] Michael Owen
 acknowledges the Newcastle fans

92
00:09:55.444 --> 00:09:57.480
as they welcome him
 to St James's Park.

93
00:09:57.564 --> 00:10:00.124
The last-minute exchange deal
 with Real Madrid

94
00:10:00.204 --> 00:10:04.516
will see Santiago Munez move
 to Real Madrid on a two-year contract.

95
00:10:08.924 --> 00:10:11.916
- Excuse me. You know where Roz is?
 - Down to the left.

96
00:10:12.004 --> 00:10:13.357
Thank you.

97
00:10:14.364 --> 00:10:18.676
There's that git,
 upsetting my lovely Rosalind.

98
00:10:18.764 --> 00:10:20.959
You're in the bad books now.

99
00:10:21.044 --> 00:10:23.512
- Hey, you save your breath, Mr lves.
 - Baby.

100
00:10:23.604 --> 00:10:26.038
- I don't want to talk to you.
 - I tried to call.

101
00:10:26.124 --> 00:10:29.514
- You should've asked for more time.
 - I tried. Hey, listen.

102
00:10:29.604 --> 00:10:33.563
I love you. I love you and I want
 to marry you. None of that changes.

103
00:10:33.644 --> 00:10:36.681
Now, before we have kids
 and responsibilities, we can...

104
00:10:36.764 --> 00:10:39.358
- Stop playing with the bed.
 - I'm sorry.

105
00:10:39.444 --> 00:10:43.403
We can go places, do things.
 Just you and me.

106
00:10:46.764 --> 00:10:50.200
I'm not sure I want to live in Spain.
 I mean...

107
00:10:50.724 --> 00:10:53.682
- I love Newcastle.
 - I love it too. It's been good to me.

108
00:10:53.764 --> 00:10:57.643
If I hadn't come I wouldn't have found
 the most important thing in my life:

109
00:10:57.724 --> 00:11:01.114
- You.
 - He's got a point there.

110
00:11:01.204 --> 00:11:05.914
Yeah, and what about our wedding and
 our new house and my job? I love my job.

111
00:11:06.004 --> 00:11:08.393
- I know, but...
 - I've got exams at Easter.

112
00:11:08.484 --> 00:11:12.238
You can see me on your days off,
 how's that? I'll fly back when I can.

113
00:11:12.324 --> 00:11:16.203
Baby, I can't walk away
 from this chance.

114
00:11:16.284 --> 00:11:21.597
This is my life,
 and I want you there... with me.

115
00:11:22.764 --> 00:11:25.836
- I can't even speak Spanish.
 - I'll teach you.

116
00:11:30.044 --> 00:11:31.443
I'm not eating paella.

117
00:11:33.804 --> 00:11:36.682
Hey, hey, hey. Come here.

118
00:11:38.244 --> 00:11:42.681
Will you do us a favour?
 When you see that Gavin Harris,

119
00:11:42.764 --> 00:11:45.232
tell him he's shite.

120
00:12:00.684 --> 00:12:04.677
- I love you.
 - I love you.

121
00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:00.875
A very good day to all of you

122
00:13:01.364 --> 00:13:04.162
and thank you for coming

123
00:13:04.604 --> 00:13:08.643
to this very important presentation

124
00:13:08.964 --> 00:13:11.603
of one of the greatest players
 in the world

125
00:13:12.124 --> 00:13:13.603
Good luck in this team.

126
00:13:14.004 --> 00:13:15.881
Best wishes
 and we place our hopes in you.

127
00:13:15.964 --> 00:13:17.443
Many thanks.

128
00:13:26.524 --> 00:13:31.473
Over ten thousand fans turned up
 to welcome Real's latest signing...

129
00:13:33.964 --> 00:13:38.162
Newcastle United fans are still coming
 to terms with the loss of Santiago,

130
00:13:38.244 --> 00:13:41.475
two years before the end
 of his contract...

131
00:13:46.564 --> 00:13:50.603
...in exchange for Michael Owen
 has shocked fans...

132
00:13:50.684 --> 00:13:55.314
...the Mexican-born striker runs
 the risk of sitting on the bench.

133
00:13:56.244 --> 00:13:57.962
How much do you think this one cost?

134
00:13:58.404 --> 00:13:59.883
I couldn't care less
 if the Bernabeu goes bankrupt.

135
00:13:59.964 --> 00:14:03.001
We have the best strikers.
 We all know that.

136
00:14:03.084 --> 00:14:05.518
They compete with each other.

137
00:14:05.604 --> 00:14:08.676
No player wants
 to be on the bench for a long time.

138
00:14:08.764 --> 00:14:11.836
I'm sure it's not that
 different for Mr Munez.

139
00:14:11.924 --> 00:14:16.873
Well, I've always been a fan of Real
 Madrid. Me, my grandma, my brother.

140
00:14:16.964 --> 00:14:20.434
It's like a dream come true for me
 to be playing on this team, yeah.

141
00:14:21.164 --> 00:14:22.517
Goal!

142
00:14:22.604 --> 00:14:25.072
Is it true only a year ago
 you were a gardener?

143
00:14:25.164 --> 00:14:29.999
I'm from a simple background. My story's
 different than most of the players.

144
00:14:30.084 --> 00:14:33.201
- Rosa. Rosa!
 - For me, it's a big thing.

145
00:14:33.284 --> 00:14:34.683
A big responsibility.

146
00:14:34.764 --> 00:14:37.437
The omelette. It's lunchtime.

147
00:14:37.524 --> 00:14:39.560
I'll try to be at the same level.

148
00:14:39.644 --> 00:14:43.557
It's an honour to play with great
 players like Zidane and David,

149
00:14:43.644 --> 00:14:46.238
Roberto Carlos, everybody, so...

150
00:14:46.324 --> 00:14:49.157
You're prepared
 for everything about to hit you?

151
00:15:12.964 --> 00:15:16.798
- First day of school. Make me proud.
 - I will, Mama.

152
00:16:46.364 --> 00:16:48.559
- Miss Harmison?
 - Hey.

153
00:16:52.004 --> 00:16:55.201
Where have you been?
 Training or shopping? Oh, my God.

154
00:16:55.284 --> 00:16:58.993
- It's for us, baby. It's for us.
 - Have they given you all this?

155
00:17:00.644 --> 00:17:03.602
- Wow. Can I have one?
 - Sure. They're for you.

156
00:17:05.964 --> 00:17:08.398
Pick a car. Any car.

157
00:17:08.484 --> 00:17:11.794
- You'll have to score a lot of goals.
 - I'll try.

158
00:17:13.244 --> 00:17:17.476
The UEFA Champions League is back,
 and it's back at the Santiago Bernabeu.

159
00:17:17.564 --> 00:17:20.954
What a stage
 for Europe's top club competition.

160
00:17:24.324 --> 00:17:26.679
- Hey.
 - Look at this.

161
00:17:26.764 --> 00:17:28.720
Oh, my God.

162
00:17:30.404 --> 00:17:32.281
Look at that.

163
00:17:32.364 --> 00:17:36.676
Real Madrid, nine times winners.
 But not now for four years.

164
00:17:36.764 --> 00:17:39.995
This is where they kick off
 their latest campaign.

165
00:17:40.084 --> 00:17:43.918
An unhappy time for Gavin Harris.
 He has a point to prove.

166
00:17:44.844 --> 00:17:46.880
- Cheers. Good luck.
 - Cheers.

167
00:17:54.884 --> 00:17:58.843
The new boy, Munez.
 He starts from the bench.

168
00:18:19.844 --> 00:18:24.042
Gavin Harris. He hasn't scored
 for 14 games. The wait goes on.

169
00:18:24.124 --> 00:18:25.842
Half a yard behind, isn't he?

170
00:18:46.884 --> 00:18:49.193
Just over half an hour to go.

171
00:18:50.484 --> 00:18:52.520
Again the delivery. No finish.

172
00:18:56.244 --> 00:19:00.795
Harris again trying to influence
 proceedings. He's struggling tonight.

173
00:19:08.164 --> 00:19:10.519
One on one,
 that should have been a goal.

174
00:19:18.604 --> 00:19:21.323
Harris off the mark, off his game.

175
00:19:23.804 --> 00:19:26.955
And the crowd's starting
 to get on the Englishman's back.

176
00:19:27.924 --> 00:19:30.961
- Oh, yeah, look, there he is.
 - It's time for a new star.

177
00:19:31.044 --> 00:19:33.797
Does this spell the end
 for Gavin Harris?

178
00:19:38.084 --> 00:19:42.043
It's certainly the start
 of something new for Santiago Munez.

179
00:19:42.804 --> 00:19:44.715
- Go, Sant.
 - Go on, Santi.

180
00:19:53.404 --> 00:19:57.113
Munez ghosting in.
 He's looking menacing.

181
00:20:01.404 --> 00:20:05.602
Oh, dear, it's all coming to the boil.
 Thomas Gravesen's brought his handbag.

182
00:20:06.324 --> 00:20:08.599
Beckham's corner.

183
00:20:08.684 --> 00:20:11.357
Not cleared,
 only as far as Munez.

184
00:20:11.444 --> 00:20:13.514
Could this be the moment?!

185
00:20:16.524 --> 00:20:18.480
Yes! Yes!

186
00:20:27.684 --> 00:20:31.836
It could not be a better start
 to his Real Madrid career.

187
00:20:31.924 --> 00:20:34.119
A last-minute goal for Santiago Munez.

188
00:20:46.364 --> 00:20:47.399
- Enrique!
 - Come on, come on.

189
00:20:47.764 --> 00:20:49.356
- Did you bring the dough?
 - Quick, before they catch us.

190
00:20:49.564 --> 00:20:50.997
OK, OK, this is for you
 and this is for me.

191
00:20:52.884 --> 00:20:54.203
What's in that head of yours?

192
00:20:54.284 --> 00:20:57.082
What do you want?
 For us to visit you in jail?

193
00:20:57.324 --> 00:20:58.313
Listen...

194
00:20:59.044 --> 00:21:03.196
...one false move,
 and you will ruin your life forever.

195
00:21:03.284 --> 00:21:04.876
More ruined than it already is?

196
00:21:06.204 --> 00:21:08.957
Enrique my love, don't say that.

197
00:21:10.244 --> 00:21:11.962
Look at that player, Munez.

198
00:21:12.684 --> 00:21:14.993
He didn't have anything, like you.

199
00:21:15.284 --> 00:21:16.603
Look at him now.

200
00:21:16.844 --> 00:21:20.439
Apart from that, what the hell
 does that have to do with me?

201
00:21:23.284 --> 00:21:27.641
I'm going to tell you a secret.
 That player is your brother.

202
00:21:30.204 --> 00:21:32.354
Santi! Over here!

203
00:21:33.124 --> 00:21:35.957
- OK, OK. Take it easy.
 - Santi!

204
00:21:36.604 --> 00:21:40.074
- Come on out, darling.
 - Careful. Are you all right?

205
00:21:40.164 --> 00:21:42.678
- Are you OK?
 - I broke my heel off.

206
00:21:44.284 --> 00:21:48.197
Come on inside. I've got a little
 surprise for you. This way.

207
00:21:50.284 --> 00:21:51.273
That's for you.

208
00:21:51.964 --> 00:21:54.762
Come on in. And follow me. Follow me.

209
00:21:58.284 --> 00:21:59.717
That's for you.

210
00:22:01.084 --> 00:22:03.075
- Come on. This way.
 - What was that?

211
00:22:03.164 --> 00:22:05.200
Come on. Patience.

212
00:22:06.524 --> 00:22:10.199
And pick her up. She can't walk.

213
00:22:24.004 --> 00:22:25.437
And that's for you.

214
00:22:28.564 --> 00:22:31.522
Come here.
 I think he wants a photo.

215
00:22:31.604 --> 00:22:33.356
Here we go.

216
00:22:35.484 --> 00:22:40.035
- So is it always like this or what?
 - It is, actually. They're all mad.

217
00:22:41.044 --> 00:22:43.842
- Total lunatics.
 - You don't sound surprised.

218
00:22:43.924 --> 00:22:46.996
- You love it.
 - What, being in the press?

219
00:22:47.084 --> 00:22:50.156
I'll tell you what.
 At the end of the day,

220
00:22:50.244 --> 00:22:54.283
I'd rather be out with my friends having
 a nice meal, nice conversation.

221
00:22:55.404 --> 00:22:57.156
Let it breathe for one minute.

222
00:22:57.244 --> 00:23:00.919
OK. There's more
 to life than just football.

223
00:23:01.004 --> 00:23:03.393
What, like computer games?

224
00:23:03.484 --> 00:23:07.033
- Come on, you're in the first team.
 - Don't get me wrong.

225
00:23:07.124 --> 00:23:10.912
It pays the bills. I do love it,
 but I've got other interests as well.

226
00:23:13.444 --> 00:23:16.004
I mean, for example, wine.

227
00:23:17.204 --> 00:23:21.880
I've made an investment
 in a tasty little vineyard in France.

228
00:23:24.284 --> 00:23:27.037
Could be my future, you know?

229
00:23:29.124 --> 00:23:34.039
- I think it's corked.
 - No, no, it's Covio de Special Reserve.

230
00:23:49.484 --> 00:23:51.839
Jump on the plane with us.
 No one will know.

231
00:23:51.924 --> 00:23:56.793
- I think the coach might notice.
 - The house is so empty without you.

232
00:23:56.884 --> 00:24:00.433
- It's only a couple of weeks.
 - I don't want to go.

233
00:24:00.524 --> 00:24:03.675
- It'll be like you never left.
 - I love you.

234
00:24:03.764 --> 00:24:05.322
Me too.

235
00:24:08.444 --> 00:24:10.958
- I'll call you, OK?
 - OK.

236
00:24:15.084 --> 00:24:18.156
- Anything you need, give me a ring.
 - Thank you.

237
00:24:31.124 --> 00:24:33.843
ONE MONTH LATER

238
00:25:04.084 --> 00:25:06.393
Sant, I'm desperate for the toilet.

239
00:25:39.884 --> 00:25:42.273
Look at the pool,
 at the gorgeous pool.

240
00:25:42.364 --> 00:25:44.559
Hey, happy birthday.

241
00:25:44.644 --> 00:25:48.637
- Didn't need to. I've got everything.
 - I won't bother next time. 29 again?

242
00:25:48.724 --> 00:25:51.079
Watch it.

243
00:25:51.164 --> 00:25:53.280
I really need a wee.
 Where's the toilet?

244
00:25:53.364 --> 00:25:55.082
- Back here.
 - See you in a minute.

245
00:25:55.164 --> 00:25:58.236
In that room.
 It's a bit of a wait, I'm afraid.

246
00:25:59.684 --> 00:26:01.720
What do you think?
 It's not bad, is it?

247
00:26:01.804 --> 00:26:03.795
Different class. How can you afford?

248
00:26:03.884 --> 00:26:06.000
I don't know.
 Barry sorts all that out.

249
00:26:06.084 --> 00:26:08.644
Hey, Barry! How can I afford this?

250
00:26:08.724 --> 00:26:12.034
Because I get you
 80 grand a week, you plank.

251
00:26:12.124 --> 00:26:15.480
Oh, yeah.
 It's because I'm on 80 grand a week.

252
00:26:15.564 --> 00:26:17.122
I've got something for you.

253
00:26:17.204 --> 00:26:20.082
Off you pop then, treacle.
 Santi, what's up, man?

254
00:26:20.164 --> 00:26:24.476
Listen, you scored an absolute belter
 tonight, love. You smashed it, bubba.

255
00:26:24.564 --> 00:26:27.601
Listen. What're you thinking
 bringing Roz up here?

256
00:26:27.684 --> 00:26:32.360
This is what we call a bona fide
 singles party, do you get me?

257
00:26:32.444 --> 00:26:35.561
- She's my fiancee.
 - Hey, Barry. Hey.

258
00:26:35.644 --> 00:26:39.273
Chateauneuf du Pape 1982.
 See what you think of that.

259
00:26:39.364 --> 00:26:42.242
- Nice.
 - Come on. Let's go outside.

260
00:26:42.324 --> 00:26:45.999
Oh, Santi.
 I've got a little idea for you, love.

261
00:26:49.364 --> 00:26:51.753
- Who's that?
 - No idea.

262
00:26:51.844 --> 00:26:53.800
So how many rooms is this?

263
00:26:53.884 --> 00:26:57.160
I think it's eight.
 But I've only been in six.

264
00:26:57.244 --> 00:27:00.873
I'm leasing it,
 and one of the rooms was locked...

265
00:27:06.964 --> 00:27:09.603
Well, but it's sort of,
 like, a little bit weird.

266
00:27:09.684 --> 00:27:11.800
It's those Euro-style bathing suits.

267
00:27:11.884 --> 00:27:13.920
I don't think I'll wear it.

268
00:27:14.004 --> 00:27:16.677
- Hey, monkey.
 - Hello.

269
00:27:17.244 --> 00:27:20.475
- Where you been?
 - Introduce me to your friend?

270
00:27:20.564 --> 00:27:24.477
Who, him?
 Jordana Garcia, Santiago Munez.

271
00:27:24.564 --> 00:27:27.522
- She can't resist me.
 - I'll try.

272
00:27:28.084 --> 00:27:29.073
Hi, Santiago.

273
00:27:29.524 --> 00:27:30.513
Hi, how are you?

274
00:27:32.164 --> 00:27:33.882
Hmm, Dolce?

275
00:27:34.964 --> 00:27:35.953
Dolce, yes, yes.

276
00:27:36.324 --> 00:27:37.473
Really good goal, eh?

277
00:27:37.564 --> 00:27:40.078
Thanks, but I only played
 for seven minutes, so I wasn't...

278
00:27:40.404 --> 00:27:42.156
Well, you must be really tired then?

279
00:27:44.484 --> 00:27:47.396
Lovely ass. I want him.

280
00:27:47.484 --> 00:27:50.396
- But I thought he had a girlfriend.
 - And who cares?

281
00:28:03.044 --> 00:28:07.083
Roz. Hiya, darling.
 It's so great to see you.

282
00:28:07.164 --> 00:28:09.280
Have you seen Santi?

283
00:28:09.364 --> 00:28:12.197
I think he just
 popped upstairs with Gav.

284
00:28:12.284 --> 00:28:14.673
- You look absolutely splendid.
 - Thank you.

285
00:28:14.764 --> 00:28:18.120
- Can I get you a drink?
 - No. I'm going to find Santi.

286
00:28:18.204 --> 00:28:20.320
- See you later.
 - See you.

287
00:28:24.844 --> 00:28:27.312
There you are.
 I've been looking everywhere.

288
00:28:27.404 --> 00:28:30.237
- Hi.
 - Roz, this is Jordana.

289
00:28:30.324 --> 00:28:31.518
- Hello.
 - Hi.

290
00:28:31.604 --> 00:28:34.482
He was telling me about your wedding.
 You're lucky.

291
00:28:34.564 --> 00:28:36.361
- Not as lucky as he is.
 - True.

292
00:28:36.444 --> 00:28:39.641
- Can we go in? It's a bit cold.
 - Yeah. Sure.

293
00:28:39.724 --> 00:28:41.919
OK, then,
 you'll have to come on my TV show

294
00:28:42.004 --> 00:28:43.756
before the other channels grab you, no?

295
00:28:43.844 --> 00:28:47.234
Well, thanks,
 but I'm not into all that stuff.

296
00:28:47.324 --> 00:28:49.440
Did you just say no to me?

297
00:28:51.884 --> 00:28:54.523
You'll like it.

298
00:28:55.844 --> 00:28:58.802
I've been cornered by Barry.
 It was disgusting.

299
00:28:58.884 --> 00:29:01.557
He's such a lech.
 His hands were all over me.

300
00:29:02.884 --> 00:29:05.876
She walked around
 without a top all night. She's a slut.

301
00:29:05.964 --> 00:29:10.355
- Glad we're home. That was mad.
 - Gavino sure was in his element.

302
00:29:10.444 --> 00:29:14.801
What did you think of that TV girl?

303
00:29:14.884 --> 00:29:17.523
- TV girl? Who?
 - You know who I mean.

304
00:29:17.604 --> 00:29:22.314
The one, "Did you just say no to me?"
 Her? Silly cow. Think she's hot?

305
00:29:23.404 --> 00:29:27.283
Don't you pause! What do you mean?
 You just paused! You can't say yes.

306
00:29:27.364 --> 00:29:30.276
She's OK. I think Gavino
 has a thing for her, actually.

307
00:29:30.364 --> 00:29:33.595
- She definitely likes you.
 - I'm irresistible, what can I do?

308
00:29:33.684 --> 00:29:36.562
I don't think so.
 I could take you or leave you.

309
00:29:36.644 --> 00:29:38.316
- I can change that.
 - Do you?

310
00:29:38.404 --> 00:29:39.439
I think so, yeah.

311
00:29:46.524 --> 00:29:48.754
Sant, why are we here?

312
00:29:51.164 --> 00:29:53.837
This is our house.

313
00:29:53.924 --> 00:29:56.040
- You've bought it?
 - Yeah, I did.

314
00:29:56.124 --> 00:29:59.673
- Oh, you haven't.
 - Yeah. What do you think? Come.

315
00:29:59.764 --> 00:30:00.753
Sant!

316
00:30:02.644 --> 00:30:05.556
- Look.
 - Oh, my God, it's massive.

317
00:30:05.644 --> 00:30:10.274
Look at the size of it.
 It's beautiful. It's amazing.

318
00:30:10.924 --> 00:30:14.200
Oh, wow! I like the kitchen.

319
00:30:14.284 --> 00:30:16.957
- It's great.
 - Yeah.

320
00:30:17.044 --> 00:30:20.957
This house belonged to a very
 famous designer. What's his name?

321
00:30:21.044 --> 00:30:24.195
Well, they say he's
 gonna be the next Versace.

322
00:30:24.284 --> 00:30:29.199
A lot of the things inside
 and the furniture were designed by him.

323
00:30:29.284 --> 00:30:31.434
- We have seven bedrooms...
 - Seven?

324
00:30:31.524 --> 00:30:34.960
- Yeah. And seven bathrooms. Cheers.
 - Cheers.

325
00:30:37.764 --> 00:30:42.679
- Do you like it?
 - Don't know what to say.

326
00:30:43.924 --> 00:30:46.643
Santi! Santi! Sant!

327
00:30:58.644 --> 00:31:00.839
I'd like to talk for a second
 about this new arrival,

328
00:31:00.924 --> 00:31:02.642
the Mexican Santiago Munez

329
00:31:02.724 --> 00:31:05.477
who we see here entering
 this restaurant looking very handsome.

330
00:31:05.564 --> 00:31:06.997
He's also a total fashion victim.

331
00:31:08.324 --> 00:31:10.758
- He'll be worse in the future.
 - I really like his style.

332
00:31:11.204 --> 00:31:12.637
Is he more Prada, or more Dolce?

333
00:31:12.724 --> 00:31:14.555
Well, we'll have to keep an eye on him.

334
00:31:14.724 --> 00:31:15.998
He'll be Dolce & Gabbana.

335
00:31:16.084 --> 00:31:17.233
I'm betting on Prada.

336
00:31:18.004 --> 00:31:19.483
I'm not sure his girlfriend
 will help much.

337
00:31:19.564 --> 00:31:21.043
She looks pretty, if a bit pale but...

338
00:31:49.564 --> 00:31:53.079
- Hello.
 - Hello, pet.

339
00:31:53.164 --> 00:31:56.634
- Hey, Mom, how are you?
 - Oh, I'm fine.

340
00:31:56.724 --> 00:31:59.716
You're in all the magazines over here.

341
00:31:59.804 --> 00:32:04.275
- Are they new shoes you're wearing?
 - Yes, Mom.

342
00:32:04.364 --> 00:32:07.595
- Were you talking to Victoria?
 - I don't even know her.

343
00:32:07.684 --> 00:32:10.721
Oh, David's looking gorgeous.

344
00:32:11.644 --> 00:32:13.282
- Listen, love.
 - Yes, Mom?

345
00:32:13.364 --> 00:32:17.152
I think you need to let
 your hair down, pet. And, Roz...

346
00:32:17.244 --> 00:32:18.518
What, Mom?

347
00:32:18.604 --> 00:32:21.323
Well, you could do
 with a bit of a spray tan.

348
00:32:56.444 --> 00:32:58.753
...immobility...

349
00:33:02.804 --> 00:33:06.001
- Darling, I'm trying to study.
 - You can study on the plane.

350
00:33:06.084 --> 00:33:09.235
I can't. I've got to get this finished.

351
00:33:09.324 --> 00:33:13.158
- But I won't see you for two weeks.
 - I know.

352
00:33:13.244 --> 00:33:15.917
Please. Can you watch TV or something?

353
00:33:40.804 --> 00:33:43.876
- It's me, you idiot.
 - Sorry, it didn't sound like you.

354
00:33:43.964 --> 00:33:47.400
- You busy?
 - I'm always busy, monkey.

355
00:33:47.484 --> 00:33:49.998
I'm at the hotel
 and they're not letting us out.

356
00:33:50.084 --> 00:33:53.281
It's a funny farm here.
 I'm locked up with a bunch of dimwits.

357
00:33:53.364 --> 00:33:55.878
- You should feel at home then.
 - Seriously.

358
00:33:55.964 --> 00:33:59.081
How about sneaking in?

359
00:33:59.164 --> 00:34:01.837
You could come up
 in one of them laundry baskets.

360
00:34:01.924 --> 00:34:05.553
Not tonight.
 I need my beauty sleep. I look awful.

361
00:34:07.044 --> 00:34:08.318
Oh, shut it!

362
00:34:09.844 --> 00:34:12.153
- Who else is there?
 - Iker, Guti,

363
00:34:12.244 --> 00:34:16.123
- Ivan, Munez.
 - Can you put Munez on?

364
00:34:17.044 --> 00:34:18.523
Munez!

365
00:34:25.724 --> 00:34:28.158
Iker, grow up.

366
00:34:32.764 --> 00:34:34.277
Yes. Santi speaking.

367
00:34:34.724 --> 00:34:35.713
Hi, Santiago, yes.

368
00:34:36.444 --> 00:34:38.719
The thing is, my producers are crazy
 about having you on the show.

369
00:34:38.804 --> 00:34:41.955
And I told them that, as a personal
 favour, you would give me the exclusive.

370
00:34:42.964 --> 00:34:44.283
Hm, I don't know.

371
00:34:46.004 --> 00:34:47.437
You're not afraid, are you?

372
00:35:07.684 --> 00:35:10.642
Hey, Gavino! Open this! Hey! Please!

373
00:35:21.044 --> 00:35:25.674
Another important UEFA Champions
 League night for Real Madrid.

374
00:35:25.764 --> 00:35:29.200
Whoever you are in this competition,
 no matter how big or small,

375
00:35:29.284 --> 00:35:31.036
it's vitally important...

376
00:35:31.124 --> 00:35:34.480
You could pay someone
 to do that for you. Professionals.

377
00:35:34.564 --> 00:35:39.194
I like doing it, Mom.
 Makes the place feel like home.

378
00:35:39.844 --> 00:35:43.439
His head is bound to be full of a
 million different things right now.

379
00:35:43.524 --> 00:35:46.322
- You should be one of them.
 - I've got to be here.

380
00:35:46.404 --> 00:35:49.760
They need me at the hospital.
 Even if I was, I couldn't see him.

381
00:35:49.844 --> 00:35:52.312
He's locked in hotels most of the week.

382
00:35:52.404 --> 00:35:56.841
What's the point of having this classy
 house if there's only you in it, pet?

383
00:36:00.204 --> 00:36:04.117
I'm serious, love. It may only
 be a few hundred miles to Madrid,

384
00:36:04.204 --> 00:36:07.435
but if you let it,
 it could become a world away.

385
00:36:18.164 --> 00:36:19.916
What is that?!

386
00:36:44.044 --> 00:36:45.636
Nice shot!

387
00:37:41.244 --> 00:37:42.996
Enrique, clean the ashtrays.

388
00:37:43.444 --> 00:37:45.196
No, I'm watching the football.

389
00:37:45.644 --> 00:37:47.236
When they pay you to watch TV,
 you'll be loaded.

390
00:37:47.324 --> 00:37:49.360
Until then, get up and work,
 like everybody else.

391
00:39:25.084 --> 00:39:27.917
Santiago Munez, super sub!

392
00:39:28.004 --> 00:39:31.792
How long can the calls for a start
 be resisted by the manager?

393
00:39:54.444 --> 00:39:56.594
- Good goal, man.
 - You OK?

394
00:39:56.684 --> 00:40:00.643
Mr Harris, what's going on with you?
 You were a disaster.

395
00:40:00.724 --> 00:40:03.522
Are you ever going
 to score another goal?

396
00:40:03.604 --> 00:40:08.724
Yeah. At this moment in time,
 I am a very bad player.

397
00:40:17.124 --> 00:40:19.354
Hey, coach?

398
00:40:19.444 --> 00:40:23.039
- Munez.
 - Can I have a word?

399
00:40:23.124 --> 00:40:24.477
Sure.

400
00:40:24.564 --> 00:40:28.159
Well, I'm feeling great.
 I'm fit, I'm scoring goals

401
00:40:28.244 --> 00:40:31.634
and I think I'm ready
 to start a full game.

402
00:40:31.724 --> 00:40:34.796
When you are ready to start, Munez,

403
00:40:34.884 --> 00:40:37.398
I promise you,
 you'll be the first to know.

404
00:40:58.244 --> 00:41:01.714
Hey, baby. You won't believe
 what I just bought for us.

405
00:41:01.804 --> 00:41:05.797
- Go on.
 - Guess. Come on!

406
00:41:05.884 --> 00:41:09.638
- I don't know, Sant.
 - Come on, come on!

407
00:41:09.724 --> 00:41:11.760
I'm not really in the mood for games.

408
00:41:12.524 --> 00:41:17.120
Lamborghini. White convertible Spyder.
 Different class.

409
00:41:18.204 --> 00:41:19.637
Roz?

410
00:41:20.604 --> 00:41:23.198
Mr lves died this morning.

411
00:41:26.844 --> 00:41:30.837
I was gonna phone you,
 but I didn't want to bring you down.

412
00:41:33.204 --> 00:41:36.002
- I'm sorry, baby.
 - I've got to go.

413
00:42:12.524 --> 00:42:16.073
Do you think Munez
 is ready for a full game?

414
00:42:16.164 --> 00:42:17.563
I think it's too early.

415
00:42:29.044 --> 00:42:31.080
Maybe you should think again.

416
00:42:44.244 --> 00:42:46.041
What's wrong with you, man?
 Can't you see I almost killed you!

417
00:42:46.284 --> 00:42:47.683
My name is Enrique, I'm your brother.

418
00:42:48.244 --> 00:42:49.438
What?

419
00:42:49.524 --> 00:42:50.673
My mother married your father,

420
00:42:50.764 --> 00:42:52.914
Hernan Munez in Mexico.

421
00:43:17.084 --> 00:43:20.713
The client's screaming down my throat.
 I don't know what I'll say.

422
00:43:23.324 --> 00:43:25.838
Mr Munez, I'm glad
 you could make it, sir.

423
00:43:25.924 --> 00:43:27.118
Do you mind?

424
00:43:28.604 --> 00:43:30.959
We're going
 straight through to the studio.

425
00:43:31.044 --> 00:43:34.832
- How long will it take?
 - Not too long if we go straight though.

426
00:43:34.924 --> 00:43:37.597
- Rolling.
 - 104, take 27.

427
00:43:37.684 --> 00:43:39.163
And action!

428
00:43:40.524 --> 00:43:42.799
That's why I go
 for Total Tofu every time.

429
00:43:42.884 --> 00:43:46.433
"The super food for the super sub."

430
00:43:52.884 --> 00:43:54.078
All right, cut!

431
00:43:54.924 --> 00:43:56.835
Great. That was great.

432
00:43:56.924 --> 00:43:59.518
One more time, then, Santiago.

433
00:44:00.324 --> 00:44:02.474
Did you do that?

434
00:44:04.324 --> 00:44:06.394
Well, it says here you did, Phil.

435
00:44:07.484 --> 00:44:09.361
- Santiago!
 - Hey, Glen.

436
00:44:09.444 --> 00:44:12.004
These people are making
 a fool out of me, man.

437
00:44:12.084 --> 00:44:14.678
- Who, Sant?
 - This commercial.

438
00:44:14.764 --> 00:44:18.200
David Beckham gets Gillette,
 and I get freaking... tofu?

439
00:44:18.284 --> 00:44:22.641
You got to start somewhere, Santiago.
 It's good money. You shouldn't complain.

440
00:44:22.724 --> 00:44:23.952
No, it's disgusting!

441
00:44:24.044 --> 00:44:27.480
You try eating it for five hours.
 Give me a break. Please.

442
00:44:27.564 --> 00:44:31.000
- I'll have a word with...
 - You know what? I'm better than this.

443
00:44:32.204 --> 00:44:35.799
- Jesus.
 - Was that Santiago?

444
00:44:37.004 --> 00:44:39.040
Aye, it was.

445
00:44:39.124 --> 00:44:42.753
For the first time this season,
 Van der Merwe has a decision to make.

446
00:44:42.844 --> 00:44:45.358
He's got Santi Munez and Gavin Harris,

447
00:44:45.444 --> 00:44:49.278
and Gavin appears to have been
 on his holidays this season.

448
00:44:49.364 --> 00:44:51.798
You're talking five million
 for the boy.

449
00:44:51.884 --> 00:44:55.001
At the moment, it doesn't
 look like he's worth a fiver to me.

450
00:45:15.004 --> 00:45:18.121
- Hey.
 - Surprise!

451
00:45:23.884 --> 00:45:25.636
I'm glad to see you.

452
00:45:27.964 --> 00:45:30.762
Cheeky git.
 He just ran in front of the car?

453
00:45:30.844 --> 00:45:32.072
There you go.

454
00:45:34.444 --> 00:45:38.039
Are you all right?
 You look a bit in shock. Hey.

455
00:45:38.124 --> 00:45:41.321
Come on, it'll be all right.
 Eat your dinner.

456
00:45:46.524 --> 00:45:49.516
Well, did he say anything else?

457
00:45:49.604 --> 00:45:51.993
No, nothing.
 When he threw that at me,

458
00:45:52.084 --> 00:45:55.201
I was so freaked I just drove off.
 I couldn't breathe.

459
00:45:55.284 --> 00:46:00.039
It might not be bad. You always
 talked about wanting to find her.

460
00:46:00.124 --> 00:46:04.322
I know. But right now, I can't deal with
 it. In my head, she was gone forever.

461
00:46:06.604 --> 00:46:08.879
She does really look like you.

462
00:46:24.164 --> 00:46:26.359
- Hey.
 - Santiago.

463
00:46:26.444 --> 00:46:29.083
- Where did you get this?
 - Is it her, Grandma?

464
00:46:30.324 --> 00:46:34.602
When you went to Spain,
 I worried this might happen.

465
00:46:34.684 --> 00:46:36.481
Wait, you knew?

466
00:46:36.564 --> 00:46:40.842
I couldn't tell you, Santiago.
 I didn't want to cause you pain.

467
00:46:40.924 --> 00:46:43.199
My God. You didn't tell me?

468
00:46:43.284 --> 00:46:46.515
- What gave you the right?
 - That woman left all of us.

469
00:46:46.604 --> 00:46:50.392
She just walked away.
 Left your father in pieces.

470
00:46:50.484 --> 00:46:52.440
But it's my choice.
 She's my mother.

471
00:46:52.524 --> 00:46:55.721
She abandoned you.
 How can you forgive her for that?

472
00:46:55.804 --> 00:46:58.193
OK, Grandma. Let me decide, please.

473
00:47:27.004 --> 00:47:29.074
Santi! Santi! Santi!

474
00:48:07.924 --> 00:48:09.835
Santi, you listening?

475
00:48:26.844 --> 00:48:28.994
It's a very big night
 for that young man.

476
00:48:29.084 --> 00:48:32.838
Santiago Munez, for the first time
 since his move from Newcastle,

477
00:48:32.924 --> 00:48:35.836
starts a game for Real Madrid.

478
00:48:35.924 --> 00:48:39.075
Illustrious company alongside him,
 to say the least.

479
00:48:39.164 --> 00:48:41.632
Just look at those names.

480
00:48:45.404 --> 00:48:50.114
They tend to be feisty, these encounters
 between Real Madrid and Valencia.

481
00:48:52.004 --> 00:48:54.234
It's Beckham forward early on.

482
00:48:54.324 --> 00:48:56.918
He's picked out Munez.
 Raul alongside him,

483
00:48:57.004 --> 00:48:59.837
but Munez goes
 for goal and glory himself.

484
00:48:59.924 --> 00:49:02.518
Wanted the glory,
 but I don't think Raul's happy.

485
00:49:02.604 --> 00:49:04.560
Perhaps he wanted that one squared.

486
00:49:06.244 --> 00:49:07.723
Raul!

487
00:49:09.804 --> 00:49:12.637
Ramos back to clear off the line.

488
00:49:12.724 --> 00:49:14.760
David Beckham now.

489
00:49:14.844 --> 00:49:18.359
Just about hooked away by Valencia.
 Under a bit of pressure here.

490
00:49:18.444 --> 00:49:24.235
But now they can counter. Picked up by
 Vicente, taken down by Santi Munez.

491
00:49:24.324 --> 00:49:28.442
Now Munez could be in real trouble here.
 He is! It's a red card.

492
00:49:28.524 --> 00:49:32.517
Munez sent off
 on his first start for Real Madrid.

493
00:49:32.604 --> 00:49:34.720
Well, it's unbelievable, isn't it?

494
00:49:34.804 --> 00:49:37.272
That's a man who's rusty.
 A late challenge.

495
00:49:37.364 --> 00:49:42.563
He gave the referee nowhere to go.
 Vicente was really clipped down.

496
00:49:42.644 --> 00:49:44.555
And it's a sad day for Munez.

497
00:49:44.644 --> 00:49:47.477
From dreams to nightmares
 for Santi Munez.

498
00:49:47.564 --> 00:49:50.681
His first start,
 and now his first early bath.

499
00:49:52.724 --> 00:49:56.353
Off comes Zinedine Zidane,
 and it's Gavin Harris who will come on.

500
00:50:02.324 --> 00:50:05.521
Plenty of tackles flying in out there,
 and that's Guti.

501
00:50:05.604 --> 00:50:08.721
Canizares, what is he doing?
 Not just with his hair either.

502
00:50:08.804 --> 00:50:11.272
This is not a typical
 Real Madrid game, is it?

503
00:50:11.364 --> 00:50:14.561
The early sending-off
 has really set the tone for the match.

504
00:50:19.284 --> 00:50:22.356
And another effort
 blocked away by Casillas.

505
00:50:22.444 --> 00:50:24.321
And the follow-up just wide.

506
00:50:24.404 --> 00:50:27.555
Down to ten men,
 it'll be very hard work for Real Madrid.

507
00:50:27.644 --> 00:50:31.239
They have to get their passing game
 going. Beckham with a free kick.

508
00:50:31.324 --> 00:50:34.202
Even he's not quite
 found his range tonight.

509
00:50:40.524 --> 00:50:42.515
David Beckham with the cross.

510
00:50:42.604 --> 00:50:48.122
Here's Gavin Harris! Goal for
 Real Madrid! And they lead one-nil!

511
00:50:48.204 --> 00:50:49.683
The drought is over.

512
00:50:49.764 --> 00:50:53.552
That's a goal poacher's goal.
 It was a great cross by Beckham.

513
00:50:53.644 --> 00:50:56.920
Harris is there in the six-yard area
 doing what he does best,

514
00:50:57.004 --> 00:50:59.074
and stoops to conquer.

515
00:50:59.684 --> 00:51:03.518
So Real Madrid scraping home in the end,
 that late goal from Gavin Harris.

516
00:51:03.604 --> 00:51:06.402
But Santiago Munez's
 moment of madness

517
00:51:06.484 --> 00:51:08.600
nearly cost them the game,

518
00:51:08.684 --> 00:51:10.993
a red card he could
 have no excuse about.

519
00:51:11.084 --> 00:51:13.644
It was a poor foul,
 poor challenge, reckless.

520
00:51:13.724 --> 00:51:16.636
The referee had no option,
 he had to go.

521
00:51:16.724 --> 00:51:20.797
Gavin, this was your first goal
 in 17 games. How do you feel?

522
00:51:22.124 --> 00:51:26.879
It's a great day. I'm very happy.

523
00:51:28.004 --> 00:51:31.235
I'm going drinking with lots of girls.

524
00:51:31.844 --> 00:51:32.833
Good night.

525
00:51:32.924 --> 00:51:34.960
Hello, hothead.

526
00:51:35.044 --> 00:51:36.443
Hello.

527
00:51:36.524 --> 00:51:39.038
Look, I have the solution
 to all your problems.

528
00:51:39.884 --> 00:51:40.919
Really?

529
00:51:42.124 --> 00:51:43.637
Tequila, please.

530
00:51:44.604 --> 00:51:46.720
And I need you on my show tomorrow

531
00:51:46.804 --> 00:51:48.920
whilst you're still
 playing for Madrid.

532
00:51:53.444 --> 00:51:54.923
You won't give up, will you?

533
00:51:56.484 --> 00:51:57.883
What do you think?

534
00:52:06.524 --> 00:52:07.559
Another?

535
00:52:07.644 --> 00:52:08.918
Another please.

536
00:52:10.484 --> 00:52:11.678
You started it. I didn't.

537
00:52:12.724 --> 00:52:13.713
Do you need a ride?

538
00:52:14.244 --> 00:52:15.313
No, thanks.

539
00:52:23.564 --> 00:52:26.124
- Bye.
 - Bye.

540
00:52:37.964 --> 00:52:41.036
Sant? Darling?

541
00:52:42.484 --> 00:52:44.475
Sweetheart, wake up.

542
00:52:45.204 --> 00:52:49.038
Come on, sleepyhead. Darling?

543
00:52:49.124 --> 00:52:52.275
Look, I've brought you breakfast.
 Do you want some juice?

544
00:52:52.364 --> 00:52:55.561
You've been asleep for ages. Here.

545
00:52:56.004 --> 00:52:58.723
- Sant.
 - Why didn't you wake me up?

546
00:52:58.804 --> 00:53:01.523
- I tried. You were dead to the world.
 - Try harder!

547
00:53:01.604 --> 00:53:04.072
- I told you to wake me up!
 - I tried...

548
00:53:04.164 --> 00:53:07.156
You stupid?
 I'm gonna miss the team plane!

549
00:53:07.244 --> 00:53:09.280
I'm not stupid. I'm not an alarm clock!

550
00:53:17.924 --> 00:53:22.122
- Hi. Trondheim, first class.
 - OK. I'll see what I can do.

551
00:53:28.574 --> 00:53:31.532
Excuse me. I got it, I got it.

552
00:53:31.614 --> 00:53:34.412
Excuse me. Sorry.

553
00:53:34.494 --> 00:53:36.450
Sorry. Sorry about the peanuts.

554
00:53:42.174 --> 00:53:43.607
It's been a good one, Santi.

555
00:53:43.694 --> 00:53:45.969
The coach sends his apologies
 for not coming to greet you

556
00:53:46.054 --> 00:53:48.170
but I know he's very keen to see you.

557
00:54:14.534 --> 00:54:16.889
Please! What is he doing?

558
00:54:32.854 --> 00:54:34.287
Warm up.

559
00:54:49.054 --> 00:54:50.965
Welcome to Norway.

560
00:54:57.054 --> 00:55:00.569
- Not such a great day, son.
 - Hey.

561
00:55:01.734 --> 00:55:06.524
I got a call from the boss. There'll be
 repercussions. Hefty fine probably.

562
00:55:08.134 --> 00:55:11.729
Nil-nil and he had me sitting
 on my freezing ass for 90 minutes.

563
00:55:11.814 --> 00:55:14.772
He's the coach, son. He calls the shots.

564
00:55:16.214 --> 00:55:18.569
He's sending a message.
 You should listen.

565
00:55:18.654 --> 00:55:21.885
Don't patronise me.
 I'm doing commercials for goddamn tofu

566
00:55:21.974 --> 00:55:26.047
- and you're fixing cars in Newcastle.
 - I'm always there for you, son.

567
00:55:26.134 --> 00:55:30.173
Well, I need someone full-time
 in Madrid to support me off the pitch.

568
00:55:31.334 --> 00:55:33.723
Well, perhaps this is where I get off.

569
00:55:40.334 --> 00:55:42.723
It's been a great ride, Santi.

570
00:55:43.414 --> 00:55:45.211
It's been a privilege.

571
00:55:49.054 --> 00:55:53.570
Your plate's getting so full so fast,
 watch what falls off the edge.

572
00:56:01.294 --> 00:56:02.966
Roz?

573
00:56:25.694 --> 00:56:30.563
I don't know what you're saying,
 but I love it.

574
00:56:31.534 --> 00:56:33.126
Careful!

575
00:56:34.614 --> 00:56:35.729
Come on, open up.

576
00:56:37.654 --> 00:56:39.292
Come on, open.

577
00:56:40.974 --> 00:56:42.293
Come on, open, we're peeing ourselves.

578
00:56:46.774 --> 00:56:48.048
Come on, open up.

579
00:56:58.774 --> 00:57:02.050
Girls? I'm going
 to have to take you home.

580
00:57:03.214 --> 00:57:04.488
What?

581
00:57:04.574 --> 00:57:06.132
Where do you live?

582
00:57:12.094 --> 00:57:14.005
I'm coming!

583
00:57:18.294 --> 00:57:21.092
- Any room at the inn?
 - Gavino?

584
00:57:24.614 --> 00:57:26.286
You're a diamond.

585
00:57:31.574 --> 00:57:33.963
So how long you gonna need to stay?

586
00:57:35.894 --> 00:57:38.966
- Quite a while, I'd imagine.
 - As long as you need, man.

587
00:57:39.054 --> 00:57:43.172
The vineyard was a scam.

588
00:57:43.254 --> 00:57:46.132
Barry? Not a very good agent.

589
00:57:55.494 --> 00:57:59.567
Hey, Santi! Where's the milk?!

590
00:58:10.134 --> 00:58:13.365
Would sir like one lump or two
 with his tea?

591
00:58:22.734 --> 00:58:25.612
- I don't know why she's so angry.
 - You can understand.

592
00:58:25.694 --> 00:58:28.527
I mean, she's up there
 all alone in that big house.

593
00:58:28.614 --> 00:58:31.048
You're out
 with dark-haired beauties.

594
00:58:31.134 --> 00:58:34.410
But I'm not out
 with dark-haired Spanish beauties.

595
00:58:34.494 --> 00:58:38.282
No, I'm just saying, you know, she can
 only imagine the worst, can't she?

596
00:58:38.374 --> 00:58:42.003
Yeah. But I've never given her
 any reason to imagine the worst.

597
00:58:42.094 --> 00:58:43.846
Yeah, I know.

598
00:58:43.934 --> 00:58:48.405
But you're an
 international Latin sex symbol.

599
00:58:48.494 --> 00:58:51.452
She knows how many girls
 have got your photo on the wall.

600
00:58:53.134 --> 00:58:56.012
That's part of the job.
 She could try to understand.

601
00:58:57.094 --> 00:59:00.325
I don't know. I'll talk to her
 during the Christmas break.

602
00:59:03.574 --> 00:59:06.327
Stop mucking about.
 You Latinos are always diving.

603
00:59:06.414 --> 00:59:09.008
- I can't. It really hurts.
 - What, you serious?

604
00:59:09.094 --> 00:59:11.130
Yeah! It really hurts.

605
00:59:19.574 --> 00:59:22.213
Don't worry about it, man,
 I'm sure it's nothing.

606
00:59:26.214 --> 00:59:29.445
You're not to set foot outside
 of this facility or your home.

607
00:59:29.534 --> 00:59:32.492
But I have travel plans
 for the Christmas break, coach.

608
00:59:32.574 --> 00:59:35.134
You're going nowhere.

609
00:59:35.214 --> 00:59:37.330
Do we have an understanding?

610
00:59:40.974 --> 00:59:42.692
I hope so.

611
00:59:47.694 --> 00:59:51.926
I don't understand. Why are they keeping
 you there? You can't do any training.

612
00:59:52.014 --> 00:59:55.165
They pay me. They call the shots.
 I cannot change that.

613
00:59:55.254 --> 01:00:00.009
- It's not fair. You promised.
 - Why don't you come here?

614
01:00:00.094 --> 01:00:03.006
All the times I've been to Madrid,
 you've not come home.

615
01:00:03.094 --> 01:00:06.006
Not set foot in Newcastle.
 This is another excuse.

616
01:00:06.094 --> 01:00:08.289
You can't call Glen, you sacked him.

617
01:00:08.374 --> 01:00:10.126
I'm getting sick of it!

618
01:00:10.214 --> 01:00:12.523
Baby, it's out of my hands. I'm sorry.

619
01:00:12.614 --> 01:00:15.651
Look, I don't want
 to speak to you right now, OK?

620
01:00:21.414 --> 01:00:25.407
There, there, Roz, pet.
 Have a nice glass of champagne.

621
01:00:27.614 --> 01:00:30.686
- Thanks.
 - It's a shame Santi couldn't be here.

622
01:00:30.774 --> 01:00:33.607
He's probably partying
 with Galacticos in Spain.

623
01:00:33.694 --> 01:00:35.969
Look at the size of this bad boy.

624
01:00:39.134 --> 01:00:40.533
Let's see if you can guess what this is.

625
01:00:40.614 --> 01:00:41.933
It isn't easy.

626
01:00:43.774 --> 01:00:45.366
It's the original Champions League ball.

627
01:00:45.454 --> 01:00:47.763
I miss you too, Gran.

628
01:00:47.854 --> 01:00:49.845
You watching The Great Escape?

629
01:00:51.814 --> 01:00:55.170
What, Steve McQueen?
 I know, he's a dish.

630
01:00:55.934 --> 01:00:58.732
OK. Big kiss.

631
01:00:58.814 --> 01:01:00.293
Bye.

632
01:01:05.174 --> 01:01:06.732
Merry Christmas.

633
01:01:08.774 --> 01:01:10.332
Merry Christmas.

634
01:01:28.374 --> 01:01:32.731
We can't get to the phone, but if you
 leave a message, we'll call you back.

635
01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:35.248
Hey, it's me.

636
01:01:35.334 --> 01:01:38.246
I can't believe
 we're not together on New Year's Eve.

637
01:01:39.854 --> 01:01:41.890
Remember the party last year?

638
01:01:41.974 --> 01:01:44.807
Jamie told me that was
 the night Keanu was conceived.

639
01:01:44.894 --> 01:01:48.364
I don't know how he can remember, but...

640
01:01:48.454 --> 01:01:51.890
Hey, listen, I love you.

641
01:01:52.534 --> 01:01:54.172
I miss you.

642
01:01:56.374 --> 01:01:58.330
Well, happy New Year.

643
01:02:19.654 --> 01:02:20.928
Hey, Sant. Sant.

644
01:02:22.054 --> 01:02:23.169
Come on.

645
01:02:31.694 --> 01:02:33.764
- Who was that?!
 - Him!

646
01:02:40.094 --> 01:02:43.882
I've heard there's a tradition
 in Spain which involves...

647
01:02:44.774 --> 01:02:47.891
...having a grape for every...

648
01:02:47.974 --> 01:02:50.807
Hang on. Hang on. Don't be greedy.

649
01:02:50.894 --> 01:02:54.284
...having a grape for every single dong
 when it goes on the...

650
01:02:54.374 --> 01:02:56.365
You want some as well? OK.

651
01:02:56.454 --> 01:02:59.844
Oh, dear, what's it gonna sound like?
 Aunt Annie?

652
01:03:00.294 --> 01:03:03.525
So you have one grape
 for every dong when it goes.

653
01:03:03.614 --> 01:03:05.923
So we've got four minutes and...

654
01:04:01.174 --> 01:04:02.687
What?

655
01:04:03.774 --> 01:04:05.492
I didn't say anything.

656
01:04:11.134 --> 01:04:14.763
No, but you were looking
 at me like that. With a look.

657
01:04:15.414 --> 01:04:19.123
- No, I wasn't.
 - Nothing happened.

658
01:04:21.414 --> 01:04:22.893
OK.

659
01:04:25.414 --> 01:04:27.325
Nothing happened.

660
01:04:45.854 --> 01:04:47.572
Do you think I look like him?

661
01:04:48.454 --> 01:04:50.490
Yes, yes, I see it now.

662
01:04:50.574 --> 01:04:52.087
Really?

663
01:04:52.174 --> 01:04:53.892
Your face and his ass.

664
01:05:07.934 --> 01:05:10.402
You've broken my window.

665
01:05:11.214 --> 01:05:13.887
Enrique, I'm telling your mother.

666
01:05:16.094 --> 01:05:17.527
Idiot!

667
01:05:36.374 --> 01:05:37.443
Need a ride?

668
01:05:38.494 --> 01:05:39.529
OK.

669
01:06:10.094 --> 01:06:11.243
Well, where do you live?

670
01:06:11.894 --> 01:06:12.929
Straight ahead.

671
01:06:19.694 --> 01:06:20.683
Who's she?

672
01:06:20.774 --> 01:06:22.002
My girlfriend.

673
01:06:22.094 --> 01:06:23.288
Leave it.

674
01:06:24.374 --> 01:06:26.046
Nice.

675
01:06:26.614 --> 01:06:28.286
Don't break them.

676
01:06:29.094 --> 01:06:30.288
Do you like football?

677
01:06:30.374 --> 01:06:31.363
Yes.

678
01:06:34.734 --> 01:06:36.326
So tell me about your mother.

679
01:06:37.054 --> 01:06:38.692
What is she saying,
 what is she doing?

680
01:06:38.774 --> 01:06:41.004
Well, she's a drag
 but I keep away from her.

681
01:06:44.294 --> 01:06:45.613
Leave it, man.

682
01:06:47.534 --> 01:06:49.047
Hey, Mr Bunderguey.

683
01:06:49.134 --> 01:06:50.283
Will you give me a tryout?

684
01:06:50.614 --> 01:06:52.013
Wait, you're calling the coach!

685
01:06:52.094 --> 01:06:54.050
Do you want me to get in trouble?
 What's your problem?

686
01:06:54.134 --> 01:06:56.045
I don't have anything.
 I live in poverty,

687
01:06:56.134 --> 01:06:57.123
and my parents work all day

688
01:06:57.214 --> 01:06:58.488
to save the business

689
01:06:59.534 --> 01:07:01.013
but I have a brother who's an idiot

690
01:07:01.094 --> 01:07:02.163
and who does nothing for me.

691
01:07:13.654 --> 01:07:14.689
What's in the bag?

692
01:07:15.654 --> 01:07:16.928
Nothing, my things.

693
01:07:21.934 --> 01:07:23.811
Enrique!

694
01:07:25.774 --> 01:07:27.207
Enrique!

695
01:08:05.054 --> 01:08:06.692
Where did you get that?

696
01:08:07.094 --> 01:08:08.686
My brother gave it to me.

697
01:08:11.654 --> 01:08:14.452
You know we can't be part of his life.

698
01:08:15.414 --> 01:08:17.882
But he's my brother,
 why do I have to keep him a secret?

699
01:08:18.254 --> 01:08:19.812
Because in this house you do as I say!

700
01:08:20.494 --> 01:08:22.086
I shouldn't have told you.

701
01:08:23.254 --> 01:08:24.369
Forget about him.

702
01:08:25.614 --> 01:08:27.172
You're not part of his world.

703
01:09:33.174 --> 01:09:35.642
They decided to keep you on
 till Santi's fit?

704
01:09:35.734 --> 01:09:37.884
Piss off, you nonce.

705
01:09:38.894 --> 01:09:42.409
Santi. You given up
 that little nurse for Jordana?

706
01:09:42.494 --> 01:09:44.485
What did you say?

707
01:09:44.574 --> 01:09:46.644
You going to show
 your Mexican temper?

708
01:09:46.734 --> 01:09:49.373
- Come on, leave it.
 - Yeah? Yeah?

709
01:09:50.894 --> 01:09:53.283
Don't get me wrong. I'm just saying.

710
01:09:53.374 --> 01:09:56.207
Is it true? Did you fly
 all the way down here for this?

711
01:09:56.294 --> 01:09:59.889
I hope he makes it worth it, that's all.

712
01:10:02.094 --> 01:10:03.891
I wouldn't be too sure.

713
01:10:04.614 --> 01:10:06.172
Why you going home?

714
01:10:06.254 --> 01:10:07.243
Who me?

715
01:10:07.334 --> 01:10:09.290
You called me three times. Look.

716
01:10:12.294 --> 01:10:14.444
Hey, Salgado, bring a couple of birds.

717
01:10:14.534 --> 01:10:15.887
I'm in the white Lamborghini.

718
01:10:17.014 --> 01:10:18.606
What's wrong?

719
01:10:24.894 --> 01:10:25.883
Where's my Lambo?

720
01:10:25.974 --> 01:10:26.963
The keys, man?

721
01:10:27.054 --> 01:10:28.169
In the glove compartment.

722
01:10:32.494 --> 01:10:34.769
Enrique! Hey!

723
01:10:37.774 --> 01:10:38.763
Follow that car!

724
01:10:38.854 --> 01:10:40.970
- The Lamborghini?
 - Yes, follow it!

725
01:10:41.054 --> 01:10:42.533
- Like in the movies?
 - Step on it!

726
01:10:48.294 --> 01:10:49.283
These crooks.

727
01:10:49.374 --> 01:10:50.409
No, it's my brother.

728
01:10:50.494 --> 01:10:51.722
Oh, he's your brother?

729
01:10:55.454 --> 01:10:56.443
What's he doing?

730
01:11:47.574 --> 01:11:49.769
Enrique! Enrique!

731
01:12:06.374 --> 01:12:07.443
To the hospital!

732
01:12:31.054 --> 01:12:32.169
Hey, a doctor!

733
01:12:32.974 --> 01:12:33.963
Hey, a doctor!

734
01:12:34.214 --> 01:12:36.091
Straight ahead, straight ahead.

735
01:12:38.494 --> 01:12:39.927
Is he OK? Is he conscious?

736
01:12:40.014 --> 01:12:41.572
Yes.

737
01:12:42.894 --> 01:12:45.692
And so, you simply lost control?

738
01:12:45.774 --> 01:12:48.572
I told you my phone rang,
 I got distracted.

739
01:12:48.654 --> 01:12:49.769
I shouldn't have answered it.

740
01:12:50.734 --> 01:12:52.008
Who was the boy with you?

741
01:12:52.254 --> 01:12:53.926
The son of a friend of mine.
 I've already told you that too.

742
01:12:54.294 --> 01:12:55.283
Calm down.

743
01:12:55.694 --> 01:12:58.572
And how much alcohol
 did you say that you had consumed?

744
01:13:04.214 --> 01:13:06.853
Come on! Get up! Get up!

745
01:13:07.894 --> 01:13:08.883
Come on!

746
01:13:09.934 --> 01:13:12.448
- Get up!
 - It just gets better and better!

747
01:13:12.534 --> 01:13:13.603
Come on, get up!

748
01:13:14.134 --> 01:13:15.362
Get up!

749
01:13:35.174 --> 01:13:36.926
I'm just doing my job.

750
01:13:37.014 --> 01:13:39.403
He chucked my camera and my glasses.

751
01:13:39.494 --> 01:13:42.691
You write that down. Yeah?

752
01:13:42.774 --> 01:13:45.527
It's my stuff. I'm just doing my job.

753
01:13:51.734 --> 01:13:53.611
- Hello?
 - Hey.

754
01:13:53.694 --> 01:13:56.652
- I'm sorry for calling so late.
 - What's up?

755
01:13:56.734 --> 01:13:59.294
Well, I'm in a little bit
 of trouble here.

756
01:13:59.374 --> 01:14:02.366
- Actually, I really messed up.
 - What have you done?

757
01:14:02.454 --> 01:14:04.968
I hit a photographer.

758
01:14:06.334 --> 01:14:08.165
They've arrested me.

759
01:14:08.254 --> 01:14:11.485
- Where are you? You OK?
 - Yeah, yeah, I'm OK.

760
01:14:11.574 --> 01:14:15.453
- I'm not your agent anymore, remember?
 - I know. I just...

761
01:14:15.534 --> 01:14:19.083
I don't deserve this, man.
 I really don't. I'm sorry.

762
01:14:19.174 --> 01:14:23.008
Don't apologise to me,
 save it for those that need it.

763
01:14:23.094 --> 01:14:26.291
You're not a kid anymore,
 you're a grown man.

764
01:14:26.374 --> 01:14:28.842
You've earned
 a lot of praise on the pitch.

765
01:14:28.934 --> 01:14:32.973
It's time to earn some respect
 in the real world, where it matters.

766
01:14:33.054 --> 01:14:36.524
OK, I'm not coming out.
 You're on your own.

767
01:15:49.094 --> 01:15:50.322
Roz?

768
01:15:51.974 --> 01:15:54.772
- Did you know about this?
 - About what?

769
01:15:54.854 --> 01:15:56.287
It's everywhere.

770
01:16:10.574 --> 01:16:12.212
- Hey.
 - How could you?

771
01:16:12.294 --> 01:16:16.810
You didn't even have the wit to do it
 in private. You had to flaunt it.

772
01:16:16.894 --> 01:16:19.089
What are you talking about?

773
01:16:19.174 --> 01:16:22.450
You're in all the magazines,
 Sant, with that girl.

774
01:16:22.534 --> 01:16:25.094
Magazines? What girl?

775
01:16:25.174 --> 01:16:28.689
Is she why you couldn't come home?
 How long's it been going on?

776
01:16:28.774 --> 01:16:32.164
No! You're getting it wrong.
 The press twists all that stuff.

777
01:16:32.254 --> 01:16:35.724
It's in front of me. I can see
 what you've been doing. Stop lying.

778
01:16:35.814 --> 01:16:38.282
- I'm not.
 - If that's the type of girl you want,

779
01:16:38.374 --> 01:16:40.934
you can have her.
 It's fine, I don't care.

780
01:16:41.014 --> 01:16:44.643
You've made a fool out of me, Santi.

781
01:16:44.734 --> 01:16:46.326
I don't deserve this.

782
01:17:45.894 --> 01:17:50.490
Please, Roz, call me back.
 I need to talk to you. OK?

783
01:17:50.574 --> 01:17:51.893
Bye.

784
01:18:54.374 --> 01:18:57.923
Goalless after the first leg
 of this Champions League semi-final

785
01:18:58.014 --> 01:19:01.973
back at the Stade de Gerland. Now
 attention switches to the Bernabeu.

786
01:19:13.934 --> 01:19:15.572
Gavin Harris on the ball now.

787
01:19:15.654 --> 01:19:19.806
He's really improved his form lately.
 Great quick feet again.

788
01:19:31.614 --> 01:19:34.651
Robinho. Strong and powerful himself.

789
01:19:34.734 --> 01:19:36.850
Gavin Harris getting forward well.

790
01:19:41.374 --> 01:19:44.332
The stakes could not be higher
 in this Spanish capital.

791
01:20:04.254 --> 01:20:09.123
In comes Beckham's cross.
 Harris could be in. Oh, Gavin Harris!

792
01:20:12.814 --> 01:20:14.088
Nice shot!

793
01:20:14.174 --> 01:20:17.325
Gavin Harris
 is enjoying life at the moment.

794
01:20:18.814 --> 01:20:23.092
The Bernabeu rises to salute Gavin
 Harris. He's done his job out there.

795
01:20:23.174 --> 01:20:26.371
A player at the top of his game.
 And on comes Munez.

796
01:20:26.454 --> 01:20:30.970
Two months out injured.
 Five minutes to show his worth.

797
01:20:31.054 --> 01:20:34.012
He'll be looking for an early touch
 and he does well.

798
01:20:34.094 --> 01:20:36.892
Munez looking sharp.
 Immediately into the action.

799
01:20:38.214 --> 01:20:39.533
And just wide.

800
01:20:42.894 --> 01:20:45.408
Munez has opened it up for himself.

801
01:20:48.494 --> 01:20:52.248
And Munez scores!
 Now they are heading for the final.

802
01:20:52.334 --> 01:20:54.643
What a finish.
 Let it run with his front foot

803
01:20:54.734 --> 01:20:59.808
through the legs. Around the corner,
 a textbook finish into the far side.

804
01:20:59.894 --> 01:21:04.331
- It was touch-and-go tonight.
 - They had us pinned for the first 45.

805
01:21:04.414 --> 01:21:07.804
Those Lyon boys will be sick
 'cause it's a game of two halves.

806
01:21:07.894 --> 01:21:11.933
And it ain't over till the fat lady
 sings. So that's football, isn't it?

807
01:21:12.014 --> 01:21:15.768
Do you think you'll play in the final
 or will the coach choose Santiago?

808
01:21:20.014 --> 01:21:24.087
You played a fantastic game, got Real
 Madrid into the final. How do you feel?

809
01:21:24.174 --> 01:21:27.962
I'm just glad we made it.
 It's all there to play for now.

810
01:21:28.054 --> 01:21:31.251
You're buddies. It's putting
 pressure on your friendship.

811
01:21:31.334 --> 01:21:34.053
We're a team.
 But first we're friends. Thanks.

812
01:22:05.774 --> 01:22:06.763
Nice one, friends.

813
01:22:06.854 --> 01:22:09.129
I'm off!

814
01:22:09.214 --> 01:22:10.442
All right.

815
01:22:10.534 --> 01:22:12.172
Thanks.

816
01:22:12.854 --> 01:22:14.003
Take care.

817
01:22:15.094 --> 01:22:16.686
Thank you.

818
01:22:37.774 --> 01:22:39.446
Excuse me,

819
01:22:39.734 --> 01:22:41.292
have you seen this person?

820
01:22:41.734 --> 01:22:43.167
No.

821
01:22:43.934 --> 01:22:45.208
Thanks.

822
01:22:55.094 --> 01:22:56.129
Have you...?

823
01:23:00.734 --> 01:23:02.611
You'll get it tomorrow.

824
01:23:02.694 --> 01:23:06.084
Watch out, someone's coming.
 See you tomorrow.

825
01:23:06.174 --> 01:23:07.289
Hey, man.

826
01:23:08.094 --> 01:23:09.686
Have you seen this woman?

827
01:23:11.614 --> 01:23:13.366
No.

828
01:23:13.454 --> 01:23:16.287
You know,
 that's a really nice watch.

829
01:23:16.374 --> 01:23:17.966
I might know where she works.

830
01:23:42.534 --> 01:23:43.933
Isn't that...?

831
01:23:44.014 --> 01:23:45.493
I think so.

832
01:23:49.174 --> 01:23:50.493
Can I help you?

833
01:23:53.374 --> 01:23:54.489
Is Rosa here?

834
01:23:55.174 --> 01:23:56.892
Rosa.

835
01:23:58.694 --> 01:24:00.093
Rosa, come out for a minute please.

836
01:24:00.174 --> 01:24:01.368
What's going on?

837
01:24:07.734 --> 01:24:09.326
I'm sorry, gents, were closing.

838
01:24:09.974 --> 01:24:11.202
I've just ordered, man.

839
01:24:12.174 --> 01:24:13.926
What are you saying?
 We've just ordered.

840
01:24:14.014 --> 01:24:16.653
That's it for today.
 The next one's on us.

841
01:24:18.774 --> 01:24:20.366
Please, please see you tomorrow.

842
01:24:20.454 --> 01:24:21.773
We're open as usual tomorrow.

843
01:24:43.454 --> 01:24:45.206
Santiago.

844
01:25:10.494 --> 01:25:11.847
Miguel.

845
01:25:12.614 --> 01:25:14.809
This is my son.

846
01:25:27.974 --> 01:25:29.646
Why did you go? Why did you leave us?

847
01:25:30.614 --> 01:25:32.286
It's...

848
01:25:33.894 --> 01:25:36.010
It's a little hard to explain.

849
01:25:37.854 --> 01:25:39.685
It had nothing to do with any of you.

850
01:25:48.374 --> 01:25:50.888
It had everything to do with us.

851
01:25:53.214 --> 01:25:55.011
I abandoned you.

852
01:25:57.654 --> 01:26:01.727
I was walking home late one night.

853
01:26:01.814 --> 01:26:06.808
And... two men attacked me.

854
01:26:08.134 --> 01:26:11.126
One of them was your uncle.

855
01:26:12.014 --> 01:26:16.212
I... managed to get home.

856
01:26:17.774 --> 01:26:21.323
I knew then that I could never
 tell your father what happened.

857
01:26:23.654 --> 01:26:25.610
And I panicked.

858
01:26:27.694 --> 01:26:29.332
And I ran away.

859
01:26:31.774 --> 01:26:35.847
Well, yeah, but not even a call?
 To explain?

860
01:26:35.934 --> 01:26:37.367
Santiago,

861
01:26:37.454 --> 01:26:41.083
I came back three weeks later
 and you were all gone.

862
01:26:41.174 --> 01:26:45.053
And no one could tell me
 where my family had disappeared to.

863
01:26:45.134 --> 01:26:49.571
And those who could wouldn't.
 But it was too late.

864
01:26:50.814 --> 01:26:52.691
You had left Mexico.

865
01:26:55.454 --> 01:26:57.729
When I saw you on the television,

866
01:26:59.014 --> 01:27:02.484
I wanted to get in touch
 with you so much.

867
01:27:04.694 --> 01:27:07.527
But I was sure that you wished me dead.

868
01:27:09.174 --> 01:27:11.927
How could you think that?

869
01:27:12.014 --> 01:27:15.563
I was angry. My dad was angry.

870
01:27:15.654 --> 01:27:20.091
He actually died full of anger at you,
 at everything. At the world.

871
01:27:27.974 --> 01:27:29.089
He loved you very much.

872
01:27:36.334 --> 01:27:37.562
Forgive me.

873
01:27:43.134 --> 01:27:44.886
Everything's going to be OK, you'll see.

874
01:27:56.134 --> 01:27:58.489
Enrique, Enrique, look who's coming.

875
01:28:09.374 --> 01:28:10.887
Can I play?

876
01:28:10.974 --> 01:28:12.487
Of course.

877
01:28:29.894 --> 01:28:30.963
Who's that?

878
01:28:33.174 --> 01:28:34.892
It's Enrique's brother.

879
01:28:38.774 --> 01:28:40.844
Goal! Yeah!

880
01:28:58.654 --> 01:29:02.090
- What the hell are you doing?
 - Oh, nothing.

881
01:29:03.374 --> 01:29:07.731
I've been getting rashes on my face
 from some sort of allergies or something

882
01:29:07.814 --> 01:29:12.934
- and this keeps it away.
 - You have a rash on your face?

883
01:29:13.014 --> 01:29:15.847
Well, it's just a little irritation.

884
01:29:15.934 --> 01:29:18.084
That's weird, man.

885
01:29:19.934 --> 01:29:24.052
You know what? I'm going
 to be honest with you here.

886
01:29:25.494 --> 01:29:28.133
I'm getting wrinkles.

887
01:29:28.214 --> 01:29:31.251
It's not a rash, I'm just
 getting wrinkles. That's all.

888
01:29:31.334 --> 01:29:33.006
What?

889
01:29:33.094 --> 01:29:35.449
I've got creaky legs,
 I'm getting wrinkles.

890
01:29:35.534 --> 01:29:37.684
My contract's up
 at the end of the season.

891
01:29:37.774 --> 01:29:41.653
So I just thought I should do
 whatever I can. Do you know what I mean?

892
01:29:41.734 --> 01:29:45.773
'Cause I'm not yet sure what I'm
 gonna do when I'm done playing.

893
01:29:45.854 --> 01:29:49.642
So you're putting face pack on
 to extend your contract?

894
01:29:49.734 --> 01:29:52.612
Well, not really.

895
01:29:53.774 --> 01:29:57.005
I mean... kind of.

896
01:29:58.614 --> 01:30:00.172
Wow.

897
01:30:02.054 --> 01:30:05.842
Well, tell me when you're done here. OK?

898
01:30:05.934 --> 01:30:09.370
Yeah, OK.
 I'll see you later, yeah?

899
01:30:09.454 --> 01:30:10.569
Yeah.

900
01:30:17.174 --> 01:30:19.972
Grandma! Mail from Santi!

901
01:30:26.134 --> 01:30:29.729
- Who is that?
 - That's your mother and stepbrother.

902
01:30:36.054 --> 01:30:37.851
Boss?

903
01:30:37.934 --> 01:30:41.847
Listen, I'm in a meeting.
 I have to call you back.

904
01:30:47.934 --> 01:30:49.208
What is it?

905
01:30:49.294 --> 01:30:51.250
Are you starting me in the final?

906
01:30:53.534 --> 01:30:55.365
Keep me on the bench.

907
01:30:55.454 --> 01:30:57.285
Play Gavino. Please.

908
01:30:57.374 --> 01:31:01.606
If he plays well in the final he could
 make the World Cup team for England.

909
01:31:59.774 --> 01:32:02.447
If you leave a message,
 we'll call you back.

910
01:32:03.254 --> 01:32:05.609
Hey, it's me.
 You know I'm not good at this,

911
01:32:05.694 --> 01:32:10.165
but before I go out tonight
 and play the biggest game of my life,

912
01:32:10.254 --> 01:32:13.883
I wanted to call you
 because I need you to hear me out.

913
01:32:13.974 --> 01:32:17.011
Everything has turned inside out
 since I came here.

914
01:32:17.094 --> 01:32:19.005
And all this money...

915
01:32:19.094 --> 01:32:21.688
...I don't need it.
 Without you it's nothing.

916
01:32:21.774 --> 01:32:24.083
I finally met my mom.

917
01:32:24.174 --> 01:32:27.211
It's still hard to take in.
 It'll take a long time.

918
01:32:27.294 --> 01:32:30.445
But I think it might be fine now.

919
01:32:30.534 --> 01:32:33.970
I won't make excuses for what I've done.
 All I can say

920
01:32:34.054 --> 01:32:38.332
is I'm just so sorry for treating you
 like I did and for pushing you away.

921
01:32:38.414 --> 01:32:40.052
I've been a total jerk.

922
01:32:40.134 --> 01:32:44.332
I know I took my eye off the ball,
 but I want to make things right.

923
01:32:44.414 --> 01:32:47.133
I love you. Please call me.

924
01:32:47.214 --> 01:32:50.968
And, well, let me know if I can see you.

925
01:32:51.054 --> 01:32:53.045
I just want a second chance.

926
01:33:58.054 --> 01:34:01.603
Gentlemen. I'm proud of you.

927
01:34:02.534 --> 01:34:04.809
You made it.

928
01:34:04.894 --> 01:34:06.771
The Champions League final.

929
01:34:07.694 --> 01:34:11.164
I don't want you
 to forget why you're here.

930
01:34:11.254 --> 01:34:13.768
I want you to play
 as if you have nothing to lose.

931
01:34:13.854 --> 01:34:17.483
Forget the money. Forget the press.
 Forget the cameras.

932
01:34:17.574 --> 01:34:20.566
Forget everything. Enjoy.

933
01:34:26.374 --> 01:34:29.605
This is it, quite simply
 the biggest club game on the planet.

934
01:34:29.694 --> 01:34:31.127
Champions League final.

935
01:34:31.214 --> 01:34:34.251
Real Madrid against Arsenal
 and it's in the Bernabeu.

936
01:34:34.334 --> 01:34:37.849
Real Madrid feeling it's destiny
 to get their name on this trophy

937
01:34:37.934 --> 01:34:43.133
yet again in their own back yard. What a
 galaxy of stars we've got on show here.

938
01:34:43.214 --> 01:34:47.651
So many match winners on show, Bill.
 I wonder which one will be the one

939
01:34:47.734 --> 01:34:52.444
to take that trophy home. Will it be
 Thierry Henry, Fabregas, or TJ Harper?

940
01:34:52.534 --> 01:34:54.843
Look at Real Madrid,
 so many fine players:

941
01:34:54.934 --> 01:34:58.370
Beckham, Zidane, and, of course,
 the inform Gavin Harris.

942
01:34:58.454 --> 01:35:00.888
You listen to me. You watch yourself.

943
01:35:02.894 --> 01:35:07.968
It was the goals from Munez and Harris
 which got Real Madrid to the final,

944
01:35:08.054 --> 01:35:13.208
but only Harris has his place in the
 starting line-up. Munez on the bench.

945
01:35:14.374 --> 01:35:18.526
Glory within touching distance for
 footballers of Arsenal and Real Madrid.

946
01:35:18.614 --> 01:35:20.923
We're under way at the Bernabeu.

947
01:35:21.014 --> 01:35:24.131
Gavin Harris with a little touch,
 he's given it to Harper.

948
01:35:24.214 --> 01:35:27.843
Harper breaking clear for Arsenal
 in the first minute. Down he goes.

949
01:35:30.174 --> 01:35:32.165
The referee gives a penalty!

950
01:35:32.254 --> 01:35:37.453
Oh, no. Pen. I can't believe Harris was
 suckered into that. A yellow to boot.

951
01:35:37.534 --> 01:35:41.891
He lost possession to TJ Harper, tried
 to get it back. Gave away the foul.

952
01:35:41.974 --> 01:35:45.171
I'm not so sure, Bill.
 That wasn't a pen to me.

953
01:35:45.254 --> 01:35:50.009
TJ Harper will step up and take it.
 Looking for the dream start for Arsenal.

954
01:35:50.094 --> 01:35:52.085
One-nil!

955
01:35:52.854 --> 01:35:56.733
He may have dived for the penalty and
 suckered Harris, but what a penalty.

956
01:35:56.814 --> 01:36:01.729
Casillas had no chance. Low down
 to the keeper's left, the perfect pen.

957
01:36:02.414 --> 01:36:06.965
The dream final for Real Madrid
 has started to turn into a nightmare.

958
01:36:07.054 --> 01:36:09.443
Arsenal have hit the ground running.

959
01:36:09.534 --> 01:36:13.209
This is Jose Antonio Reyes
 for Thierry Henry!

960
01:36:13.294 --> 01:36:16.172
Whoa, should have scored, Thierry Henry.

961
01:36:16.254 --> 01:36:19.007
Good jump, should have
 gone back across the keeper.

962
01:36:19.094 --> 01:36:22.131
Great cross from Reyes,
 super shape. Should be two-nil.

963
01:36:22.214 --> 01:36:25.729
The stars of Real Madrid
 are being eclipsed by North Londoners.

964
01:36:25.814 --> 01:36:31.332
Henry for Reyes. Casillas again
 providing a vital save for Real Madrid.

965
01:36:31.414 --> 01:36:34.133
He's saving the Galacticos
 at the moment.

966
01:36:34.214 --> 01:36:37.809
The Arsenal youngsters
 are the ones rising to the occasion.

967
01:36:37.894 --> 01:36:41.728
Forward for Arsenal again.
 It's wave after wave of Gunners attacks.

968
01:36:41.814 --> 01:36:45.045
It's Freddie Ljungberg here.
 And out comes Casillas.

969
01:36:45.134 --> 01:36:49.844
Man of the match for Real Madrid
 in this first half, he really has been.

970
01:36:58.534 --> 01:37:01.367
Real Madrid saved, really,
 by the halftime whistle.

971
01:37:01.454 --> 01:37:06.323
It's been a torrid first 45 minutes.
 Change is surely afoot at halftime.

972
01:37:06.414 --> 01:37:09.247
Munez, go warm up. You go on.

973
01:37:11.814 --> 01:37:15.887
Hey, lady! Is she upset?

974
01:37:15.974 --> 01:37:19.410
Do you want to go? Because
 I'll tell you, I will destroy you!

975
01:37:19.494 --> 01:37:22.406
Leave it. He's not worth it.
 Easy, easy, easy.

976
01:37:22.494 --> 01:37:23.768
One-nil!

977
01:37:23.854 --> 01:37:26.652
TJ made you look like an idiot.

978
01:37:26.734 --> 01:37:29.248
I know, boss.
 Look, I know what you'll say...

979
01:37:29.334 --> 01:37:31.609
Here's what I want you to do.
 Push forward.

980
01:37:31.694 --> 01:37:34.208
I'm bringing in Santi.
 You'll play him behind.

981
01:37:34.294 --> 01:37:37.411
Now get the hell out there
 and show me some cojones.

982
01:37:37.494 --> 01:37:40.452
Here comes the change,
 but it's not quite as we thought.

983
01:37:40.534 --> 01:37:43.924
On comes Munez, but he's gonna
 come on to partner Gavin Harris.

984
01:37:44.014 --> 01:37:46.403
I don't think Arsenal
 pre-empted this one.

985
01:37:46.494 --> 01:37:50.328
I wonder how it'll work. They have to
 strike up understanding quickly.

986
01:37:50.414 --> 01:37:53.372
Not since Newcastle days
 have they lined up together.

987
01:37:56.014 --> 01:37:58.369
It's tantalisingly close now
 for Arsenal.

988
01:37:58.454 --> 01:38:01.890
Just 45 minutes away
 from winning the European Cup

989
01:38:01.974 --> 01:38:04.727
for the first time in their history.

990
01:38:04.814 --> 01:38:10.366
Fabregas finds Henry. This is a strong,
 purposeful, excellent run from Henry.

991
01:38:10.974 --> 01:38:12.692
It's majestic!

992
01:38:14.654 --> 01:38:17.248
And it's two-nil to Arsenal.

993
01:38:29.214 --> 01:38:31.125
King Henry for Arsenal.

994
01:38:31.214 --> 01:38:35.526
The captain leads them one step closer
 to European glory

995
01:38:35.614 --> 01:38:39.368
and Real Madrid have another nail
 in their coffin.

996
01:38:39.454 --> 01:38:43.493
Where's Beckham? Where's Ronaldo?
 Where's Raul? Where's Gavin Harris?

997
01:38:43.574 --> 01:38:47.533
The big names have to start
 stepping up for Real Madrid.

998
01:38:47.614 --> 01:38:49.969
Here comes Henry again.

999
01:38:50.054 --> 01:38:53.046
Goodness, he's in the mood.
 So are his teammates.

1000
01:38:53.134 --> 01:38:58.254
Cleared, but back for Thierry Henry.
 Can he get another here, Henry?

1001
01:38:58.334 --> 01:39:02.293
Goes to ground, it's come to Fabregas.
 But it's come to nothing.

1002
01:39:02.374 --> 01:39:04.888
I wonder when Real Madrid
 will get started.

1003
01:39:04.974 --> 01:39:09.445
It's all Arsenal, two-nil up and looking
 like they could go further ahead.

1004
01:39:09.534 --> 01:39:12.048
A rare Real Madrid attack. Zidane.

1005
01:39:12.134 --> 01:39:14.728
Beckham wants it,
 left-hand side. Ronaldo.

1006
01:39:14.814 --> 01:39:18.124
All names we've seen
 too little of so far.

1007
01:39:18.214 --> 01:39:20.648
Here is Ronaldo,
 but Lehmann got there first.

1008
01:39:20.734 --> 01:39:25.762
Arsenal with this run of clean sheets
 in this road to the final.

1009
01:39:25.854 --> 01:39:29.005
Looks like a road
 that will end with glory for them.

1010
01:39:29.094 --> 01:39:31.688
- Robert Pires now.
 - Clear it, clear it!

1011
01:39:32.734 --> 01:39:34.850
Again, it's Casillas.

1012
01:39:34.934 --> 01:39:39.052
And if it wasn't for Casillas, I think
 it could've been a bit of a rout.

1013
01:39:39.134 --> 01:39:41.728
Very embarrassing for Real Madrid.

1014
01:39:47.374 --> 01:39:51.492
Plenty of furrowed brows amongst
 the all-stars of Real Madrid,

1015
01:39:51.574 --> 01:39:54.646
and in this bumper crowd
 at the Bernabeu.

1016
01:39:54.734 --> 01:39:58.010
TJ Harper, who started
 the ball rolling for Arsenal,

1017
01:39:58.094 --> 01:40:02.326
sees Cicinho, forward for Real Madrid.
 Arsenal have it back.

1018
01:40:03.534 --> 01:40:08.050
Aliaksandr Hleb,
 teed up for Thierry Henry.

1019
01:40:08.134 --> 01:40:11.251
Real Madrid just can't
 get a foothold in this game.

1020
01:40:12.014 --> 01:40:14.926
Here comes Freddie Ljungberg.
 He's brought down!

1021
01:40:15.014 --> 01:40:18.245
It's gonna be another penalty
 to Arsenal. It is!

1022
01:40:18.894 --> 01:40:21.806
Real Madrid defence
 can't cope with Thierry Henry.

1023
01:40:21.894 --> 01:40:26.445
Took it down in one touch. Turned, just
 Freddie Ljungberg behind the back four.

1024
01:40:26.534 --> 01:40:29.924
And no doubt about it,
 it was a foul and it was a penalty.

1025
01:40:30.014 --> 01:40:33.802
Things are getting worse and worse
 for Real Madrid, and if this goes in,

1026
01:40:33.894 --> 01:40:39.048
three-nil and echoes of that
 Barcelona defeat last season.

1027
01:40:45.174 --> 01:40:48.246
And surely if TJ Harper
 hits the target and scores,

1028
01:40:48.334 --> 01:40:50.689
it's all over for Real Madrid.

1029
01:40:54.174 --> 01:40:58.690
Saved! Onto the bar! Casillas
 does his bit for Real Madrid again.

1030
01:41:00.054 --> 01:41:03.967
Munez looking for Harris.
 He's the furthest man up field.

1031
01:41:04.054 --> 01:41:08.013
Arsenal have been caught out here.
 Too many men committed forward.

1032
01:41:08.094 --> 01:41:11.291
Gavin Harris,
 on his own, going for goal!

1033
01:41:11.374 --> 01:41:13.763
Real Madrid are back in this final!

1034
01:41:13.854 --> 01:41:17.164
What an extraordinary turn of events.
 Arsenal disappointed.

1035
01:41:17.254 --> 01:41:19.609
It hits the bar,
 it bounds out to Munez,

1036
01:41:19.694 --> 01:41:22.162
and in one swoop,
 a ball up front to Harris,

1037
01:41:22.254 --> 01:41:25.803
a superb dip and volley over Lehmann.
 Four minutes.

1038
01:41:25.894 --> 01:41:29.807
Four very long minutes for Arsenal,
 four very short ones for Real Madrid.

1039
01:41:29.894 --> 01:41:33.853
Maybe, just maybe, they can get back
 into this game. Beckham.

1040
01:41:35.294 --> 01:41:37.967
He's picked out Harris. Munez wants it.

1041
01:41:38.374 --> 01:41:41.013
Finally, they start to combine.
 It's Munez.

1042
01:41:41.094 --> 01:41:42.607
Lehmann tips it onto the bar.

1043
01:41:42.694 --> 01:41:46.846
What a save that was. Reflexes from
 Lehmann, a close-in volley from Munez.

1044
01:41:46.934 --> 01:41:50.722
At last, Harris and Munez
 really linking up with each other.

1045
01:41:50.814 --> 01:41:52.327
These two can play together.

1046
01:41:52.414 --> 01:41:55.565
The clock ticks on.
 Gravesen looks forward for Real Madrid.

1047
01:41:55.654 --> 01:41:58.691
Arsenal, for the first time
 in the match, under pressure.

1048
01:41:58.774 --> 01:42:00.765
Here's Cicinho.

1049
01:42:00.854 --> 01:42:04.130
They know, Arsenal,
 they are in a match now.

1050
01:42:04.214 --> 01:42:06.045
Gravesen urging his teammates.

1051
01:42:06.134 --> 01:42:09.410
He knows how important it is,
 and the game can still be won.

1052
01:42:09.494 --> 01:42:11.166
Beckham's corner.

1053
01:42:14.414 --> 01:42:17.087
Lehmann punches clear.

1054
01:42:17.174 --> 01:42:19.404
Lehmann's had his problems
 with crosses,

1055
01:42:19.494 --> 01:42:22.292
but there he's really confident
 and elects to punch.

1056
01:42:22.374 --> 01:42:25.650
Into stoppage time we go.
 Two minutes at the end

1057
01:42:25.734 --> 01:42:27.964
of this Champions League final.

1058
01:42:28.054 --> 01:42:30.807
Roberto Carlos
 with a high-lofted ball.

1059
01:42:30.894 --> 01:42:34.091
Desperation time, really,
 for Real Madrid.

1060
01:42:41.614 --> 01:42:46.483
The super sub with a super goal!
 Two-two!

1061
01:42:50.414 --> 01:42:53.486
Arsenal's shell-shocked.
 The Bernabeu is rocking.

1062
01:42:53.574 --> 01:42:56.532
They really believe
 they could win this final now.

1063
01:42:56.614 --> 01:43:01.085
They've scored once in stoppage time.
 Can they do it again?

1064
01:43:05.974 --> 01:43:08.966
Guti. Harris with the touch on.

1065
01:43:09.054 --> 01:43:12.444
Here comes Santiago Munez,
 brought down.

1066
01:43:14.734 --> 01:43:16.645
Free kick, Real Madrid.

1067
01:43:32.214 --> 01:43:36.412
If there's anyone you'd want
 in this situation, it's David Beckham.

1068
01:43:36.494 --> 01:43:38.485
Cometh the moment, cometh the man.

1069
01:43:38.574 --> 01:43:42.931
It's Beckham to win the
 Champions League for Real Madrid.

1070
01:43:52.414 --> 01:43:53.767
Beckham!

1071
01:43:54.414 --> 01:43:57.053
It's looking good! It's in!

1072
01:43:57.134 --> 01:44:00.046
David Beckham has done it
 for Real Madrid!

1073
01:44:00.134 --> 01:44:03.046
They are European champions!

1074
01:44:03.134 --> 01:44:08.162
The most incredible finish in a
 Champions League final you'd ever see.

1075
01:44:08.254 --> 01:44:13.453
Beckham with the winning goal,
 Real Madrid with the winning habit!

1076
01:44:14.854 --> 01:44:18.085
They were down and out at two-nil.
 They've come back into it.

1077
01:44:18.174 --> 01:44:22.213
And it's those three who
 have led them to European glory.
